mipsgot_gcc_be.so, mipsgot_clang_el.so, mipsgot_gcc_be64.so -- MIPS PIC
shared objects whose calls and data accesses go through the primary GOT to
functions and variables the image itself defines (GH-904;
decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/src/loader/kuna_mipsgot.rs,
tests/stages/kuna-mipsgot-local.xml).

What they are
  mipsgot_gcc_be.so     o32 big-endian, gcc -O2.
  mipsgot_clang_el.so   o32 little-endian, clang -O2, linked with GNU ld.
  mipsgot_gcc_be64.so   N64 big-endian, gcc -O2 -mabi=64 -march=mips64r2.
  Source: mipsgot.c. c_add calls add64 and c_calls the weak wfn through
  their global GOT entries; c_calls reads the static counter through a local
  page entry and gdata through its global entry; c_puts loads a string's page;
  c_ptr returns the hidden hfn's local entry. Each image keeps one import, puts.

Why they are vendored
  CI has no MIPS toolchain, and the assertions read exact GOT layouts.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc 10.3.0, GNU ld 2.38 and clang 14.0.0 (host):

      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EB -fPIC -shared -nostdlib -w -O2 -Wl,--build-id=none \
          mipsgot.c -o mipsgot_gcc_be.so
      clang -target mipsel-linux-gnu -fPIC -w -O2 -c mipsgot.c -o mipsgot_clang_el.o
      mipsel-linux-gnu-ld -shared --build-id=none mipsgot_clang_el.o -o mipsgot_clang_el.so
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EB -mabi=64 -march=mips64r2 -fPIC -shared -nostdlib -w -O2 \
          -Wl,--build-id=none mipsgot.c -o mipsgot_gcc_be64.so

